from pathlib import Path
import json,hashlib
P=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
baseq=json.loads((P/'benchmark-v1/questions.json').read_text());basek=json.loads((P/'benchmark-v1/answer-key.json').read_text())
questions=baseq['questions'].copy();answers=basek['answers'].copy();additions=[]
def add(q,a,refs,novelty):
 id=f'Q{len(questions)+1:02d}'
 questions.append({'id':id,'question':q});answers.append({'id':id,'expected_answer':a.replace(' | ','; '),'required_facts':a.split(' | '),'contextual_background':[],'source_refs':refs});additions.append({'id':id,'novelty':novelty,'source_refs':refs})
add('What does Regroup draw after combat if you win versus lose? If it is your defeated sidekick’s played card and the duel continues, does that draw still occur?', 'Win draws 2 instead of 1, not 3 total | Lose draws 1 | Defeated sidekick’s played after-combat effect still resolves if duel continues', ['all four action sheets: Regroup; rulebook p12'], 'Replacement draw branch; after-combat survival interaction')
add('Your fighter plays Momentous Shift while in its turn-start space after moving away and back. Is the value 3 or 5? What if it is now in a different space from where it started this turn, including when defending on the opponent’s turn?', 'Same space as turn start means printed value 3 | Different current space from where that fighter started this turn means value 5 instead | Test uses current turn, including opponent’s turn when defending; no requirement to be attacker', ['alice-action-cards.png r3c5–6; king-arthur-action-cards.png r4c4–6; sinbad-action-cards.png r4c4–6'], 'Turn-relative spatial test and return-to-origin failure branch')
add('After Looking Glass, what choices are available, how many must be different, and can you choose the draw twice or place Alice in her current or an occupied space? If Alice is SMALL, what is the card’s defense value?', 'Choose 2 different of draw 2, recover 3 health for Alice, place Alice in any other space | Cannot choose draw twice | Placement cannot be current space or occupied space | SMALL Alice defense value 2+1=3', ['alice-action-cards.png r1c1–2; alice-character.png; rulebook p7'], 'Distinct-choice effect, placement destination and size defense application')
add('What condition enables Snicker-Snack’s after-combat hand effect, who sees the hand, who chooses the discarded card, and where does it go? What happens to that effect if Alice loses combat?', 'Requires Alice winning combat | Alice player looks at opponent’s hand and chooses 1 card opponent discards into opponent’s discard pile | No hand/discard effect on loss', ['alice-action-cards.png r1c3; rulebook p10;p12'], 'Win-only chosen discard with hand inspection and loss branch')
add('For each of O Frabjous Day!, The Other Side of the Mushroom, I’m Late I’m Late, and Mad as a Hatter, state the after-combat movement (who and maximum distance, if any) and size effect. Can these size changes alter the attack damage already resolved?', 'O Frabjous Day changes size with no movement | Other Side moves Alice up to 3 then changes size | I’m Late moves Alice up to 5 then changes size | Mad as a Hatter moves each own fighter up to 2 then changes size | All size changes mandatory and after current damage, so not retroactive', ['alice-action-cards.png r1c4–5;r2c2–4;r4c3–4; alice-character.png; rulebook p12'], 'Complete remaining size-change effects: different movement actors and timing')
add('Manxome Foe is played with printed value 3 and its during-combat discard reveals a card of combat value 5 and BOOST 2. Which card is discarded from where, what is Manxome Foe’s value before other modifiers, and does that discard count as drawing a card?', 'Discard top card of own deck during combat into own discard pile | Add BOOST 2, not combat value 5: value 3+2=5 before other modifiers | Discard is not a draw', ['alice-action-cards.png r4c5–6; rulebook p10'], 'Top-deck discard uses boost not combat value and is not draw')
add('Jabberwock uses Claws That Catch against a hero, then in a separate combat against a sidekick. What is its combat value in each case before other modifiers, and does Alice being BIG add to either?', 'Against hero value 5 instead of 3 | Against sidekick value 3 | Alice size does not modify Jabberwock’s cards', ['alice-action-cards.png r3c3–4; alice-character.png'], 'Hero versus sidekick conditional replacement value')
add('Arthur attacks with Noble Sacrifice, committing a BOOST-2 card through his ability and later discarding a BOOST-3 card through Noble Sacrifice. If uncancelled, what is the attack value and when is each boost chosen? If a defending Feint cancels Noble Sacrifice, which boosts survive and what is the attack value?', 'Ability BOOST chosen face down alongside attack before reveal | Noble Sacrifice optional extra BOOST chosen during combat | Uncancelled value 2+2+3=7 | Defending Feint cancels Noble Sacrifice effect and nullifies ability BOOST, which is discarded; no during-combat extra BOOST permitted; value remains printed 2', ['king-arthur-character.png; king-arthur-action-cards.png r1c1–3;r5c1–3'], 'Two separately timed boosts and cancellation interaction')
add('Who may play The Lady of the Lake, what named card does it retrieve from which locations to where, when must you shuffle, and what are Excalibur’s user, type and printed attack value?', 'Arthur plays Lady of Lake scheme | Search own deck and discard for Excalibur, add to hand | Shuffle deck if searched deck | Excalibur Arthur-only attack value 6', ['king-arthur-action-cards.png r1c4;r2c3'], 'Named-card search, hand destination and conditional shuffle')
add('After an uncancelled The Aid of Morgana, do you draw only if Arthur won? How many cards, at what timing, and who is allowed to play it?', 'Arthur-only attack | After combat draw 2 mandatory whether won or lost, if game continues', ['king-arthur-action-cards.png r1c5; rulebook p12'], 'Unconditional Arthur attack draw versus win-dependent effects')
add('Who can play Divine Intervention, as what combat-card type, and whom does it move how far at which timing? Must that fighter have won?', 'Arthur-only versatile usable attack or defense | After combat move Arthur up to 5; no win condition', ['king-arthur-action-cards.png r1c6;r2c1'], 'Arthur-only versatile relocation without win condition')
add('Who plays Prophecy, what happens to the top four cards, and in what order may cards be returned to the deck? Is this a scheme or an attack?', 'Merlin-only scheme | Look top 4 of own deck; add 2 to hand; return other 2 atop own deck in any order', ['king-arthur-action-cards.png r2c4'], 'Top-deck inspection with selection and ordered replacement')
add('For Bewilderment, name its legal fighter, card type and printed defense value; state its during-combat effect and optional after-combat placement, including destination occupancy. Does its printed zero automatically make the attacker win?', 'Merlin-only defense value 0 | During combat prevent all damage | After combat may place Merlin in any unoccupied space | Prevented attack damage means defender wins despite zero printed defense; zero alone does not make attacker win', ['king-arthur-action-cards.png r2c5–6; rulebook p7;p12'], 'Damage prevention overrides numerical subtraction and optional placement')
add('Who plays Aid the Chosen One, what type/value is it, and what happens after combat on a win versus a loss?', 'Merlin-only attack value 4 | If won draw 2 after combat | If lost no draw from this effect', ['king-arthur-action-cards.png r3c1'], 'Merlin win-triggered draw with failure branch')
add('For Restless Spirits, who is the active fighter, where must the chosen space be, which spaces and fighters take how much damage, and how many cards are drawn if zero, one or two opposing fighters are defeated? If the opposing hero is defeated, do you finish the draw?', 'Merlin plays scheme | Choose space in Merlin’s zone and one space adjacent to that chosen space; deal 2 to each opposing fighter in those two spaces | Zero defeated: no draw; one or two defeated: draw 1 total | Opposing hero defeated ends game immediately before further draw', ['king-arthur-action-cards.png r3c2; rulebook p14'], 'Two-space opposing-only area damage, once-only defeat trigger and end interruption')
add('Who plays Command the Storms, which fighters can it move how far, and when moving an opposing fighter which side’s fighters can it pass through and which block it?', 'Merlin-only scheme | Move each fighter including opposing up to 3 | For opposing fighter use owner perspective: can pass its friendly fighters, cannot pass its enemies; cannot end occupied', ['king-arthur-action-cards.png r3c3–4; rulebook p9'], 'Both-side movement with owner-relative blockers')
add('Can Merlin use Swift Strike, which fighter does it move, how far and when, and does it require a combat win?', 'ANY allows Merlin | After combat move the fighter that used it up to 4 | No win condition', ['king-arthur-action-cards.png r3c5–6'], 'ANY attack relocation attached to active fighter')
add('Medusa attacks using Gaze of Stone (value 2) against an uncancelled defense value 2, then in a separate combat against no defense. Assuming no other modifiers and a surviving target, state attack damage, combat winner and Gaze’s extra damage in each case.', 'Against defense 2 attack damage 0, defender wins, no Gaze extra 8 | Undefended attack damage 2, Medusa wins, after combat deal 8 extra to opposing fighter if game continues', ['medusa-action-cards.png r1c1–2;r1c4; rulebook p12;p14'], 'Large win-triggered effect blocked by tied attack and undefended branch')
add('Who plays A Momentary Glance, when does it deal how much damage, what determines its target’s location, and may it target a friendly fighter instead of an opponent?', 'Medusa-only scheme resolves its effect on scheme action | Deal 2 damage to any one fighter in Medusa’s zone | Any includes friendly; not restricted to opponents', ['medusa-action-cards.png r1c5–6'], 'Any-fighter scheme contrasted with opponent-only hero ability')
add('Who can use Hiss and Slither versus Clutching Claws, what are their card types, and what happens after combat? Must you win, and does either printed effect let you choose the opponent’s discard or make it random?', 'Hiss Medusa-only defense; Clutching Harpy-only versatile | After combat opponent discards 1 regardless of win | Neither says you choose or random; opponent discards their chosen card', ['medusa-action-cards.png r2c1–3;r2c6;r3c1–2'], 'Two restricted discard effects, default opponent selection and no win condition')
add('Who can play The Hounds of Mighty Zeus, what type and value is it, and after combat does it move just the fighting Harpy or all Harpies, for how far? Can Medusa play it herself?', 'Harpy-only versatile value 4 | After combat move each Harpy up to 3 | Medusa cannot play it', ['medusa-action-cards.png r2c4–5'], 'Harpy card moves all surviving Harpies, restricted user')
add('When may Second Shot be BOOSTed, who may use it and what is its type/base value? If you discard a BOOST-2 card, what is the attack value and what happens to the discarded card’s effect?', 'Medusa-only attack value 3 | During combat optional BOOST by discarding 1 hand card | Add 2 gives 5; ignore discarded card effect', ['medusa-action-cards.png r3c5–6;r4c1; rulebook p10'], 'Medusa card-specific during-combat attack boost')
add('Can a Harpy use Dash as defense, who moves afterward, what is the maximum movement, and must that Harpy win for the movement to occur if it survives?', 'ANY versatile permits Harpy defense | After combat move that fighting Harpy up to 3, not all fighters | No win condition', ['medusa-action-cards.png r4c2–4'], 'ANY versatile active-fighter move without win trigger')
add('Who may use Snipe and in which combat roles, and what does it do after combat on a loss as well as a win?', 'ANY fighter may use versatile Snipe attacking or defending | After combat draw 1, on loss as well as win if game continues', ['medusa-action-cards.png r4c5–6;r5c1'], 'ANY versatile unconditional draw')
add('Who may use Toil and Danger and in which combat roles, and what does it move how far at what timing? Does Sinbad’s Voyage-count maneuver bonus increase that card’s printed movement?', 'Sinbad-only versatile may attack or defend | After combat move Sinbad up to 3 | Voyage-count movement ability applies when maneuvering, so does not increase this card’s move', ['sinbad-action-cards.png r1c1–4; sinbad-character.png'], 'Card movement distinct from maneuver-only Voyage bonus')
add('Who may play Riches Beyond Compare, what action does it use, and what is its mandatory effect? With 8 cards after resolving it midturn, must you immediately discard?', 'Sinbad-only scheme | Draw 3 mandatory | No immediate hand-limit discard midturn; enforce 7 at turn end', ['sinbad-action-cards.png r1c6;r2c1; rulebook p8–10'], 'Three-card scheme draw and hand-limit timing')
add('Who may use By Fortune and Fate, what type/value is it, and what does it do after combat? If Porter is defeated but Sinbad lives, may you initiate it as an attack, and may the unusable card still BOOST?', 'Porter-only attack value 3; after combat draw 2 without win condition | Defeated Porter cannot initiate an attack with it; card still usable to pay BOOST', ['sinbad-action-cards.png r2c2–4; rulebook p10–12'], 'Porter-only attack draw and defeated-user play restriction')
add('Compare Commanding Impact and Exploit: allowed users, combat type/value, and their after-combat effects. Do their draws require winning?', 'Both ANY | Commanding Impact attack value 5; Exploit versatile value 4 | Both after combat draw 1 without win requirement', ['sinbad-action-cards.png r3c5;r4c2–3'], 'Remaining Sinbad unconditional draw cards with distinct combat roles')
add('For Leap Away, what type/value and permitted users does it have, and what happens after a win versus a loss? Which fighter can be moved how far, and do normal blockers apply if you move an opponent?', 'ANY versatile value 4 | If won after combat choose either fighter in combat and move up to 4 | Loss gives no movement | Opponent movement obeys owner-relative normal blockers and no occupied endpoint', ['sinbad-action-cards.png r3c6;r4c1; rulebook p9'], 'Long win-triggered either-combatant movement')
add('After Voyage to the Island That Was a Whale, who recovers how much health, is a combat win required, and what if Sinbad is already at 14 health or has been defeated?', 'After combat Sinbad recovers 2 without win condition | At 14 capped at 15 | Defeated Sinbad has already lost duel so cannot be saved', ['sinbad-action-cards.png r2c5; sinbad-character.png; rulebook p5;p14'], 'Voyage recovery and cap/end branches')
add('What exactly does Voyage to the Valley of the Giant Snakes do after combat, does it require a win, and does it discard a card from that hand?', 'Look at opponent’s hand after combat regardless of win | No discard effect', ['sinbad-action-cards.png r2c6'], 'Voyage hand inspection without discard')
add('What exactly happens after Voyage to the Creature with Eyes Like Coals of Fire, who loses the card, how is it selected, and is a combat win required?', 'After combat opponent discards 1 random card | No win requirement', ['sinbad-action-cards.png r3c1'], 'Random opponent discard distinct from chosen discard')
add('What movement does Voyage to the Cannibals with the Root of Madness allow after combat, who moves, is it optional, and must Sinbad have won?', 'After combat may move Sinbad up to 2 | Optional and no win requirement', ['sinbad-action-cards.png r3c2'], 'Optional Voyage movement actor and timing')
