add('What happens after Voyage to the City of the King of Serendib, when and for whose hand, and must Sinbad win first?', 'After combat draw 1 into own hand, mandatory without win requirement if duel continues', ['sinbad-action-cards.png r3c4; rulebook p9;p12'], 'Voyage draw timing and mandatory branch')
add('A required draw of 2 begins with one card left in your deck and all fighters alive. What happens to the first and second draws, does an empty deck alone deal damage before a draw is requested, and does the discard pile get shuffled?', 'First draw takes remaining card into hand | Second missing draw deals 2 to each own fighter immediately | Empty deck alone marks exhausted but deals no damage until a draw required | No reshuffle', ['rulebook p9'], 'Partially available draw and exhaustion trigger boundary')
add('Both combatants play Feint. Which immediately effect resolves first, what happens to the other Feint’s effect, and do the printed combat values vanish?', 'Defender’s immediately effect first cancels attacker Feint effects | Attacker cancellation does not resolve | Printed values remain; only effects canceled', ['all four action sheets Feint; rulebook p12'], 'Same-timing cancellation priority interaction')
